  "description": "The one-nucleon cut entropy of the Markov/Plancherel measure is the SAME number at every A (1.0359164340, to <1e-50 out to n=24), because the one-nucleon marginal of the n-strand Markov measure IS the 3-strand Markov measure -- A_(3) = [4]_q/[2]_q^3 and A_(2,1) = [2]_q/[2]_q^3 exactly. B_AME is extensive and rises 17.6x over the same range, so E_0*S_cut cannot be the binding energy and the deuteron's 1.9493x was a coincidence. SCOPE (b): the invariant is the Markov compatibility axiom, definitional not fitted.",
