  "caveats": [
    "SCOPE (b) -- a structural exclusion with a named invariant, not the usual scope-(a) negative. The invariant is Markov compatibility (M1+M3 on the tower), which is definitional rather than fitted: a compatible family has an n-independent k-strand marginal by construction, so any functional of that marginal is n-independent. Lean: QOU.MassTheory.MarkovMarginalConstant.",
    "What is excluded is THIS OBJECT -- the entropy of a fixed-width marginal of the Markov measure -- from carrying an extensive quantity. Entanglement cost is NOT excluded as an ingredient of binding, and a cut whose width GROWS with A is untouched by this argument.",
